    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d151">

                <pb facs="0237" n="971" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg971"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Sill.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-07-09"><hi rendition="#italic">July 9,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 87.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 120, diplomatic series, of the 7th ultimo, in regard to recent political
                    changes in Korea.</p>
                <p>Your action in refusing to recognize that Korean independence dates from the 6th
                    of June, 1895, is approved. The position assumed by this Government toward Korea
                    since contracting a treaty with it in 1882 has in no wise been affected by
                    recent events. Korea’s treaty independence since then has been for us an
                    established and accepted fact.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
